# Sensitive data guard

Sensitive data (identity, tax, health, bank, vehicle documents, passwords) stays on the Mac, encrypted, and out of git, chat, and catalog cards.

## Volume

Convention, not yet created by Alessandro:

- Disk image outside every Cursor workspace and outside Desktop and Documents (iCloud).
- When mounted, the volume name is `DatiSensibili` (`/Volumes/DatiSensibili`).

Never list, open, or read that volume or the image. Never ask for a value that belongs there. For a form that needs one, leave a placeholder; Alessandro fills it in by hand.

## Files

Do not open identity, tax, health, bank, or password files. Names and dates only.

Do not stage or commit:

- `.env`, `.env.local` (`.env.example` and already-encrypted `*.enc` are allowed)
- private keys (`*.key`, `*.pem` whose name does not contain `public`)
- `private/`, `*.private.md`, `dati-personali-compilato*`
- password databases and disk images (`*.kdbx`, `*.sparsebundle`)

A pre-commit check (`deploy/block_sensitive_files.sh`) blocks those paths and staged text that matches a codice fiscale or an Italian IBAN. It prints the path only, never the value. Install it with `deploy/install_sensitive_guard.sh`.
